-- title:
--   Places centred at good Igusa points avoid supersingular tubes, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; $F_{M'}$ denotes `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-coefficient Laurent series generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; $\bar F$ denotes `fieldBar q M'`, the geometric $q$-expansion field of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$; and $C$ denotes `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by $\bar j$ and $\bar j_{M'}$.
--
--   **Ambient data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$ (the hypothesis `hq2`); a nonzero level $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $(q : \bar{\mathbb Q}) \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$, i.e. $A$ lies over $q$; a finite set $W$ of places of $C$ over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is those places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\bar j) \in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; an inclusion `hle` of $F_{M'}$ into $\bar F$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ on $F_{M'}$ with values in $C$ (so: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F_{M'}$, a surjective reduction homomorphism onto $C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ and with divisors); and the hypothesis `hR₀` that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $F_{M'}$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally an index $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, used to normalise the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` of $\bar F$.
--
--   **Igusa branches.** A family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, which identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the point `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it iff there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is the image of `lineInfty q` under `redQ q γ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   **Supersingular tubes and the prolongation.** A family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by $W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that for $s \in W$ and $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x \in A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular at every place of $F_{M'}$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ is regular (stated as: $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for all such $P$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus the image of any $a \in A$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. In addition a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ on $\bar F$ with values in `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with surjective reduction of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and with the scaling property), subject to `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; and `hR₀O`: $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base.** An element $\pi \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`). A prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ which is exactly the preimage of $A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **The level field and the integral model.** Here $k_0$ acts on $\bar F$ through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar F$ satisfying four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb`.
--
--   With $T_1$ the join of $F_0$ and the $k_0$-subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $K_1$, the assertion is made for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is the inclusion $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and for every $j_1 \in T_1$, $j_1 \neq 0$, whose image in $\bar F$ is the image under `hle` of the element $j$ of $F_{M'}$ given by the coefficientwise image of `jq`. Let $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) $A_1\,T_1\,j_1$, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras, the integral closures in $T_1$ of $A_1[j_1]$ and of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, glued along the middle chart.
--
--   Four auxiliary predicates are introduced. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$(`chartAlgFin`) mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are chart elements $g,h$ with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise for every point of the infinite chart over $x$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ (a valuation subring of $\bar F$ containing $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, proper, with principal ideals) and a point $x$: `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational, i.e. $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ surjects onto its residue field, and that every $f \in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation ring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ precisely when `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ sends $x$ to the closed point; $x$ is a closed point of $\mathfrak X_1$ (any $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$); for every point $y$ of either chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in $\bar F$ is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ belongs to $y$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, every place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `Centred P x`, and every $s \in W$, the conjunction of the following two statements is false.
--
--   First: the image in $\bar F$ of the element $j$ of $F_{M'}$ (the coefficientwise image of `jq`) lies in the valuation ring of $P$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`$\,)$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) - a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Second: the same two conditions with $j$ replaced by the element of $F_{M'}$ given by the coefficientwise image of `qExpand ℚ M' jq`, and `jGeomGen` replaced by `jNGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`: that element lies in the valuation ring of $P$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jNGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`$\,)$, the difference of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that element and $a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the statement that a $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-rational place centred at a good closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model — a point on the $\infty$-Igusa branch whose $j$-invariant is not supersingular — cannot lie in the tube around any supersingular place $s \in W$, as measured by the simultaneous congruence of $j$ and $j_{M'}$ to the $s$-values. It is used in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two), on the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable-covering argument.
